/-!
# Weight-two Γ(N)-invariance of (a/b) (c/e)'

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.LevelN.slash_eq_self_of_mem_Gamma_of_mul_eq`
(`16bfc875-4874-52bf-95c1-f9b8c0a5796d`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `d1dcdfea-5846-5a00-aecd-535a05eaba65`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Fix a natural number $N$ with $N \neq 0$, and let $A_N \subseteq (\mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C})$ be the
$\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra [`ModularCurve.LevelN.ring
N`](def/ModularCurve_LevelNFunctionField.html#L28), defined as the $\mathbb{C}$-algebra generated by
the function `jAnalytic` together with all the functions `fricke N v` for $v \in (\mathbb{Z}/N)^2$
with $v \neq 0$. Let $F : \mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ be holomorphic, in the sense of being
differentiable for the standard complex-manifold structures on the upper half-plane and on
$\mathbb{C}$, and let $a, b, c, e : \mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ be four elements of $A_N$ with $b$
and $e$ not the zero function. Assume that for every $\tau \in \mathbb{H}$ one has $$F(\tau)\,
b(\tau)\, e(\tau)^2 = a(\tau)\bigl(e(\tau)\, c'(\tau) - c(\tau)\, e'(\tau)\bigr),$$ where the
derivatives are the complex derivatives at $\tau$ of the compositions of $c$ and $e$ with
`UpperHalfPlane.ofComplex`; informally, $F = (a/b)\,(c/e)'$ away from the zeros of $be$. Then for
every $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lying in the principal congruence subgroup $\Gamma(N)$,
the weight-$2$ slash action leaves $F$ unchanged: $F \mid_2 \gamma = F$ as functions on
$\mathbb{H}$.

This is the automorphy half of the classical description of differentials of the first kind on the
modular curve $X(N)$: a function of the form $(a/b)\,d(c/e)/d\tau$ with $a,b,c,e$ modular functions
of level $N$ transforms with weight $2$ under $\Gamma(N)$. It is used in the construction of an
injective linear map from regular differentials to cusp forms,
[`ModularCurve.LevelN.exists_linearMap_regularDifferentials_cuspForm_injective`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.LevelN.exists_linearMap_regularDifferentials_cuspForm_injective).

